{"content":[{"c":["CRUSE*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Small earthen vessel or flask, about four to six inches (10 to15 centimeters) tall, used for holding liquids (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.17.12-16","r":"1Kgs.17.12-16","rawR":"1Kgs.17.12-16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.17.12-16","value":"1Kgs.17.12-16"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 17:12-16"},"). In the ",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},", two other Hebrew words are translated “cruse.” However, a bottle or jar is probably in view in ",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.14.3","r":"1Kgs.14.3","rawR":"1Kgs.14.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.14.3","value":"1Kgs.14.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kings 14:3"},", and an open dish or bowl in ",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.2.20","r":"2Kgs.2.20","rawR":"2Kgs.2.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.2.20","value":"2Kgs.2.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kings 2:20"},"."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Pottery_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Pottery_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Pottery_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Pottery"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Cruse","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 17:12-16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.17.12-16","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.17.12-16","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.17.12-16"},{"anchorText":"1 Kings 14:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.14.3","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.14.3","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.14.3"},{"anchorText":"2 Kings 2:20","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.2.20","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.2.20","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.2.20"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"dc113aa8cdea595ee8bb2c3ef1443ccf0559b9e27df2a3a78665afdd555f2bc0","sourceItemName":"Cruse